Yes, you do have things to spare.  You have tons of unidentified
potions, wands, scrolls, gems, etcs.  They don't really help you at the
moment effectively.

Most of us usually 'stash' items like these.  Find a container, move it
to next to an altar.  Dump everything you don't need for the moment in
there.  You come back to the stash when you need/want to deal with
them.  It's a lot more important to be unburdened, than carry items
that you go 'I don't know what this is but it *might* save me.'

Now, identifying objects in this game is very critical part of the game
(and I find it rather fun, puzzle like).  I don't know if you want to
be spoiled, but there are spoilers.  If you want to see them, try
searching for 'nethack object identicication spoiler' or something
along that line on google.  There's a wealth of information out there.




